\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The growth hypothesis in Euclidean reconstruction}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{\citet{§3, pp. 87–88}{osterwalder1973euclidean} state their
Euclidean conditions E0–E4 and a reconstruction claim.
\citet{p. 282, and §IV.1, p. 287}{osterwalder1975euclidean}
identify the failure of the earlier Lemma 8.8 and leave open
there whether E0–E4 alone suffice. Their corrected implication
on p. 287 is cited, not proved here. It uses the strengthened
growth condition #{\mathrm{E0}^{\prime}}, or the stronger #{\mathrm{E0}^{\prime\prime}}, together with
E1–E4, and yields a unique Wightman theory with R0–R5 and the
additional growth estimate #{\mathrm{R0}^{\prime}} on its distributions.}

\p{A reflected form on one prescribed finite connection
probability, as in \ref{fdip-019N}, concerns its two
restriction domains. Reconstruction also needs the full
sequence of Euclidean functions with the stated covariance,
positivity, symmetry, clustering and growth conditions.}
